 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Pick a spot that's not right by the road, and that' out of the wind. A flat bit near the showers is usually safe. Lovely. Then stake it so it's high and not blown over. That's normal. Fold the root into the middle, then fold rest once, pull the tips tight, and tie it off with a stick. Keep it further away than the campfire rules say, at least ten metres. Exactly. And don't park near anyone else's. People are often careless with fires on hiking trips.",
